# gitleaks allowlist - xete-mcp
# Added 2026-07-31 alongside .github/workflows/gitleaks.yml (audit finding "gitleaks").
#
# One line per finding, pinned by gitleaks fingerprint:
#     <commit>:<file>:<rule-id>:<line>      for history (`gitleaks git`) scans
#     <file>:<rule-id>:<line>               for tree     (`gitleaks dir`) scans
#
# A fingerprint is exact. It cannot suppress a different secret, a different
# line, or the same line once it moves or changes commit - so an entry here
# quietly stops working instead of quietly hiding something new.
#
# The tree-scan form is matched against the path gitleaks prints, so it only
# lines up when the scan is invoked from the repo root ("gitleaks dir ." from
# the checkout, which is what .github/workflows/gitleaks.yml does). Scanning
# by absolute path produces absolute File values and these entries will not
# match - that fails closed (noisy), not open, but it is worth knowing.
#
# RULE: every entry needs a written justification saying why the value is not
# a credential. If you cannot write one, it is not a false positive - remove
# the value and rotate it instead. Do not add blanket path or rule entries.

